{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_03f981cf2c902ccc1daffcf76bae77443a3f523f337e86d69440a7abc517f042"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The user-facing input is a free-text 'intuition' (e.g. 'I think a website for dogsitters would be cool'), and an optional final step applies pivots based on user feedback."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0ab916c3efe008be414fa2ccfd5278d9020c8eb71e177e005c353323f46a595c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: to run from source, install dependencies with pip3 install -r requirements.txt (after Llama 2 access and huggingface-cli login) and run the main loop with python3 main.py; a Google Colab notebook is offered for quick testing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1f99275eda3b8e236020dc3c1e82cd1b5226701781b1edbe829d5f0a48b057b7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is described as a Llama 2 autonomous agent that devises a startup idea, business plans, and React codebases from a simple user 'intuition'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_38b485dc506ba15a8ba029d71bfdf5df6e1e021a484369752ec567cc79a63503"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent runs an idea loop: it develops a business idea and plan, iterates via a criticism loop that regenerates the plan, and asks an 'investor' prompt for approval, restarting on disapproval."},{"claim_ids":["clm_54e77c15b00d3c43644506d1fb6c9a1dc4fccf81154e07fe5415cfebc2a399a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project advertises 100% Llama 2 inference with no OpenAI keys necessary, and applies lean startup concepts such as pivots and a tight MVP build loop."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ba076d4464309fb6940ee9230e3fcd833970ecbee8d926fed397bcaf94a73e9c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The author notes the model needs a quality GPU to load the Llama 2 13b chat model, and a TODO says the React coding output needs bug fixing more often than not."},{"claim_ids":["clm_da475bc54ded7368025a0f32fe5554efa950d538fad8b614274cf1a1f0e57725"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README claims memory via vector search over historically successful ideas paired with intuitions, and that previous criticisms are used for investor approvals."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e533d32d7e4c6dbf8d6c4aae136d494851c553afa76707031aa53b93c9a0cbba"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"After plan approval, the agent generates a React codebase using the author's separate 10x-React-Engineer project."}],"claim_ids":["clm_03f981cf2c902ccc1daffcf76bae77443a3f523f337e86d69440a7abc517f042","clm_0ab916c3efe008be414fa2ccfd5278d9020c8eb71e177e005c353323f46a595c","clm_1f99275eda3b8e236020dc3c1e82cd1b5226701781b1edbe829d5f0a48b057b7","clm_38b485dc506ba15a8ba029d71bfdf5df6e1e021a484369752ec567cc79a63503","clm_54e77c15b00d3c43644506d1fb6c9a1dc4fccf81154e07fe5415cfebc2a399a4","clm_ba076d4464309fb6940ee9230e3fcd833970ecbee8d926fed397bcaf94a73e9c","clm_da475bc54ded7368025a0f32fe5554efa950d538fad8b614274cf1a1f0e57725","clm_e533d32d7e4c6dbf8d6c4aae136d494851c553afa76707031aa53b93c9a0cbba"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_2711137bccdc4533b1c1e7370bbf2e0e","id":"pg_e0507ef411425442a2f9c1a668462286","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/jawerty-autostartup-readme-md-60ec3affede5-c1a668462286.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_aa8758de49ac5a1c8536c34db7f58f23"],"title":"jawerty/AutoStartup/README.md @ 60ec3affede5","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2711137bccdc4533b1c1e7370bbf2e0e"}
